::::
---

A collection of calculators from around the web, for the [ZFS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZFS?useskin=vector) filesystem. This 
was mainly done to preserve them in one place, and to experiment with using [PyScript](https://pyscript.net/)
(allows python to be used for browser scripting instead of javascript).

If you don't know much about ZFS, or need to brush up on your knowledge, ["OpenZFS: the final word in file 
systems"](https://jro.io/truenas/openzfs/) by Jason Rose is a fantastic introduction.

`<br>`{=html}

## RAIDZ Expansion

---

The latest TrueNAS ([Electric-Eel / 24.10](https://www.truenas.com/docs/scale/24.10/gettingstarted/scalereleasenotes/))
now supports RAIDZ expansion, which allows you to append disks to an existing
vdev. This allows you to extend you're vdevs over time, rather than having to erase the vdev, create a new one, and
restore from backup. It has one small caveat however, which is that the existing data still uses the data-to-parity
ratio and block width of the old vdev size. This effectively means that you don't get the full capacity of your
drives until that existing data is rewritten.

This calculator allows you to determine how much space is lost compared to creating a new vdev from scratch.

> Credit: based on the TrueNas calculator at <https://www.truenas.com/docs/references/extensioncalculator>, which in turn
is based on [this spreadsheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1qiDPfLN-K88FMHMxcgtkxswY5Wtu7h9tBAOgJfnO7VE).

---

:::: side-by-side

:::

```=html
    <label style="display: block">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Drive Size (TB):</span>
      <input type="text" id="drive_size_input" style="width: 6rem;" />
    </label>
    <label style="display: block">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">RAIDZ Level / Number of Parity Disks:</span>
      <select id="raidz_level_input" style="width: 6rem;">
        <option value="1">1</option>
        <option value="2">2</option>
        <option value="3">3</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <label style="display: block">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Data Expansion Threshold (%):</span>
    <input type="text" id="expansion_input" style="width: 6rem;" />
    </label>
    <label style="display: block">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Initial Number of Drives:</span>
    <input type="text" id="initial_input" style="width: 6rem;" />
    </label>
    <label style="display: block">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Final Number of Drives:</span>
    <input type="text" id="final_input" style="width: 6rem;" />
    </label>
    <br>
    <button mpy-click="calculate">Calculate</button>
```

:::

:::

```=html
    <b>Extend VDEV to final width all at once</b>

    <label style="display: block; padding-left: 2rem">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Total capacity lost:</span>
      <span id="total_capacity_recovered">0%</span>
    </label>

    <label style="display: block; padding-left: 2rem">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Capacity lost:</span>
      <span id="capacity_recovered">0 TB</span>
    </label>

    <label style="display: block; padding-left: 2rem">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Capacity lost in drives:</span>
      <span id="drives_worth_recovered">0 Drives</span>
    </label>

    <b>Extend VDEV one drive at a time</b>

    <label style="display: block; padding-left: 2rem">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Total capacity lost:</span>
      <span id="total_capacity_recovered_compound">0%</span>
    </label>

    <label style="display: block; padding-left: 2rem">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Capacity lost:</span>
      <span id="capacity_recovered_compound">0 TB</span>
    </label>

    <label style="display: block; padding-left: 2rem">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 19rem;">Capacity lost in drives:</span>
      <span id="drives_worth_recovered_compound">0 Drives</span>
    </label>
```

:::

::::

```=pyscript

    from pyscript import document

    def calculate(event):
        drive_size = int(document.querySelector("#drive_size_input").value)
        raidz_level = int(document.querySelector("#raidz_level_input").value)
        expansion = float(document.querySelector("#expansion_input").value)
        initial_drives = int(document.querySelector("#initial_input").value)
        final_drives = int(document.querySelector("#final_input").value)

        expansionPercent = expansion / 100
        percentage_decrease = (final_drives-initial_drives) / final_drives
        drives_worth_recovered = expansionPercent * raidz_level * percentage_decrease
        capacity_recovered = drive_size * drives_worth_recovered
        total_capacity_recovered = drives_worth_recovered / final_drives

        l = 0
        for i in range(initial_drives + 1, final_drives + 1):
            l += 1 / i
        drives_worth_recovered_compound = expansionPercent * raidz_level * l
        capacity_recovered_compound = drive_size * drives_worth_recovered_compound
        total_capacity_recovered_compound = drives_worth_recovered_compound / final_drives
        
        span = document.querySelector("#capacity_recovered")
        span.innerText = f"{capacity_recovered:.2f} TB"
        span = document.querySelector("#drives_worth_recovered")
        span.innerText = f"{drives_worth_recovered:.2f} Drives"
        span = document.querySelector("#total_capacity_recovered")
        span.innerText = f"{total_capacity_recovered:.2%}"

        span = document.querySelector("#capacity_recovered_compound")
        span.innerText = f"{capacity_recovered_compound:.2f} TB"
        span = document.querySelector("#drives_worth_recovered_compound")
        span.innerText = f"{drives_worth_recovered_compound:.2f} Drives"
        span = document.querySelector("#total_capacity_recovered_compound")
        span.innerText = f"{total_capacity_recovered_compound:.2%}"
```
